    "question": "Must the shareholders' agreement be part of the constitutional contract?",
    "answer": "Not necessarily; the Law says it may be part of the constitutional contract or articles of association. But some provisions that are meant to have an institutional effect may require aligning the constitutional documents and completing procedures and registration according to the nature of the provision."
